```
import java.util.*; 

public class PersistentCache {
    private int capacity;
    private Map<String, Object> cache;
    private Deque<String> lruDeque;
    private Queue<String> fifoQueue;
    private Map<String, Long> timestampMap;

    private static final long DEFAULT_TTL = 3600; // 1 hour

    public PersistentCache(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
        cache = new HashMap<>(capacity);
        lruDeque = new LinkedList<>();
        fifoQueue = new LinkedList<>();
        timestampMap = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public synchronized void put(String key, Object value, long ttl) {
        // Remove expired items from the cache first
        removeExpired();

        // Check if key already exists in the cache
        if(cache.containsKey(key)) {
            // Update the value and move the key to the front of the LRU queue
            cache.put(key, value);
            lruDeque.remove(key);
            lruDeque.offerFirst(key);
        }
        else {
            // Check if the cache is full and evict an item
            if(cache.size() == capacity) {
                // Remove the least recently used item from the LRU queue
                String lruKey = lruDeque.removeLast();
                cache.remove(lruKey);
                timestampMap.remove(lruKey);
                fifoQueue.remove(lruKey);
            }

            // Add the new data item to the cache
            cache.put(key, value);

            // Add the key to the front of the LRU queue
            lruDeque.offerFirst(key);

            // Add the key to the end of the FIFO queue
            fifoQueue.offer(key);

            // Add the timestamp for the key to the timestamp map
            timestampMap.put(key, System.currentTimeMillis() + ttl);
        }
    }

    public synchronized Object get(String key) {
        // Remove expired items from the cache first
        removeExpired();

        // Check if the key exists in the cache
        if(cache.containsKey(key)) {
            // Move the key to the front of the LRU queue
            lruDeque.remove(key);
            lruDeque.offerFirst(key);
            return cache.get(key);
        }
        else {
            return null;
        }
    }

    private synchronized void removeExpired() {
        long currentTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        List<String> expiredKeys = new ArrayList<>();

        // Loop through the timestamp map to find expired keys
        for(Map.Entry<String, Long> entry : timestampMap.entrySet()) {
            String key = entry.getKey();
            Long timestamp = entry.getValue();

            if(currentTime > timestamp) {
                // Remove the expired key from all data structures
                expiredKeys.add(key);
                cache.remove(key);
                lruDeque.remove(key);
                fifoQueue.remove(key);
            }
        }

        // Remove the expired keys from the timestamp map
        for(String key : expiredKeys) {
            timestampMap.remove(key);
        }
    }
}
```

In the above code snippet, a synchronized `put()` method is used to insert data into the cache, while a synchronized `get()` method is used to retrieve data from the cache. The `put()` method first removes any expired data from the cache using the `removeExpired()` method, which checks the timestamp map for any expired data and removes them. It then checks if the key already exists in the cache, updates the value and moves it to the front of the LRU queue. If the key is not present, the method checks if the cache is full, and if so, removes the least recently used item from the LRU queue, and FIFO queue followed by updating the timestamp in the timestamp map for the new data item. The new data item is then added to the cache and its key is added to the front of the LRU queue, the end of the FIFO queue, and the timestamp map.

The `get()` method also removes any expired data from the cache before checking if the key exists in the cache. If the key is present, the method moves it to the front of the LRU queue and returns the corresponding value. If the key is not present, the method returns null.

This example code shows how a persistent cache data structure can be implemented using the combined policies of LRU, FIFO, and TTL to achieve efficient memory usage and optimized data storage.

