  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Responsive Hero Section Template</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/tachyons@4.11.1/css/tachyons.min.css">
  <style>
    .hero {
      height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      background: linear-gradient(to bottom right, #5c0099, #00d4ff);
      animation: gradient 15s ease infinite alternate;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 3rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .hero p {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .cta {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      border: 2px solid white;
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 1rem 2rem;
      color: white;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: all 0.4s ease;
    }

    .cta:hover {
      background-color: white;
      color: #5c0099;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .hero h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .hero p {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
      }

      .cta {
        font-size: 1rem;
        padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem;
      }
    }

    @keyframes gradient {
      0% {
        background-position: 0 0;
      }

      100% {
        background-position: 100% 100%;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Hero Section Title</h1>
    <p>Here's a brief description of the product or service.</p>
    <a href="#" class="cta">Call-to-Action Button</a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

Explanation:

- The `hero` class is used to set the height of the section to 100% of the viewport and to center the content vertically and horizontally using flexbox. 
- The `background` property sets a linear gradient from purple to blue, which is animated using the `animation` property (the `gradient` keyframe animation specifies that the background position should move from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner over a 15-second period, and then back to the top-left corner again).
- The `color` property sets the text color to white to contrast with the gradient background. 
- The `cta` class is used for the call-to-action button, and has some basic styles for a border, padding, and font size. The `transition` property is used to animate the color change when the button is hovered over, and the `cursor` property is set to `pointer` to provide visual feedback to the user.
- The `@media` rule is used to apply some responsive styles to the text and button at smaller screen sizes. 
- Finally, the `font-size` and `margin` properties are used to tweak the size and spacing of the heading and subheading.

